    "name": "Server Configuration API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "API to manage server-wide configuration that is mutable at runtime without a restart. Each\nconfiguration section is stored under a well-known name. A section is read as three layers:\n`readOnly` (declarative, fixed at boot), `writable` (runtime-mutable, set via `PUT`), and\n`merged` (the effective value in use, derived from the other two). The concrete shape of a\nsection's value is section-specific.\n",
      "type": "text/plain"
